Description:

Chunked HTTP bodies with an out-of-range, empty, or otherwise malformed chunk
size are now rejected.  Previously the size was parsed into a 32-bit value
that silently truncated, so a declared size just above the 32-bit range became
zero -- the marker for the last chunk -- and the body that followed it stayed
in the stream to be read as the beginning of the next request.

Tracked as GitHub security advisory GHSA-v5r2-7989-g575.

